[{"location":"mps_guide/#MPS-based-Fibonacci-Chain-Implementation","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"This document describes the MPS (Matrix Product State) implementation for Fibonacci chain measurements using ITensor.","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Overview","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Overview","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"The MPS implementation provides an efficient way to handle larger system sizes compared to exact diagonalization, while maintaining high accuracy for ground state properties and measurement dynamics.","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Key-Features","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Key Features","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/#1.-Ground-State-Generation","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"1. Ground State Generation","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"fibonacci_mps_ground_state(N; pbc=true): Generates the ground state of the Fibonacci chain using DMRG\nReturns both the MPS state and ground state energy\nSupports periodic boundary conditions (PBC) and open boundary conditions (OBC)","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#2.-Measurement-Operators","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"2. Measurement Operators","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"measurement_operator_mps(sites, i, τ, sign; pbc=true): Creates measurement operators as MPO\nSupports both :p (plus) and :m (minus) measurement outcomes\nHandles boundary conditions and local measurement rules","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#3.-State-Evolution","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"3. State Evolution","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"apply_measurement_mps(ψ, sites, i, τ, sign; pbc=true): Applies measurement to MPS state\nReturns the evolved state and measurement probability\nAutomatically normalizes the resulting state","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#4.-Sampling-and-Enumeration","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"4. Sampling and Enumeration","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"mps_sampling(ψ, sites, measurement_sites, τ; num_samples=1000, pbc=true): Monte Carlo sampling\nmps_measurement_enumeration(ψ, sites, measurement_sites, τ; pbc=true): Exact enumeration\nmps_bulk_measurement(ψ, sites, N, τ, D; pbc=true): Bulk measurement with alternating pattern","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#5.-Entanglement-Analysis","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"5. Entanglement Analysis","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"calculate_entanglement_entropy_mps(ψ, b): Calculates von Neumann entanglement entropy at bond b","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Usage-Examples","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Usage Examples","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Basic-Ground-State-Calculation","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Basic Ground State Calculation","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"using FibonacciChain\n\n# Generate ground state for 10-site chain\nN = 10\nψ, energy = fibonacci_mps_ground_state(N; pbc=true)\nprintln(\"Ground state energy: $energy\")\nprintln(\"Bond dimensions: $(linkdims(ψ))\")","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Single-Measurement","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Single Measurement","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"# Get site indices\nsites = siteinds(ψ)\n\n# Apply measurement at site 2\nτ = 1.0\nψ_measured, prob = apply_measurement_mps(ψ, sites, 2, τ, :p; pbc=true)\nprintln(\"Measurement probability: $prob\")","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Sampling-Measurements","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Sampling Measurements","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"# Define measurement sites\nmeasurement_sites = [2, 4, 6, 8]\nnum_samples = 1000\n\n# Perform sampling\nsamples, weights = mps_sampling(ψ, sites, measurement_sites, τ; \n                               num_samples=num_samples, pbc=true)\n\n# Analyze results\nprintln(\"Average weight: $(sum(weights)/length(weights))\")","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Entanglement-Entropy","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Entanglement Entropy","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"# Calculate entanglement entropy at different cuts\nfor b in 2:(N-1)\n    ee = calculate_entanglement_entropy_mps(ψ, b)\n    println(\"EE at cut $b: $ee\")\nend","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Comparison-with-Exact-Diagonalization","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Comparison with Exact Diagonalization","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"Aspect Exact Diagonalization MPS\nSystem Size Limited (~20 sites) Large (>100 sites)\nMemory Usage Exponential Polynomial\nGround State Exact Highly accurate\nMeasurements Exact probabilities Accurate probabilities\nEntanglement Exact Accurate","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Performance-Considerations","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Performance Considerations","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Bond-Dimension","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Bond Dimension","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"Controls the accuracy vs. computational cost trade-off\nDefault maximum bond dimension: 200\nCan be adjusted in DMRG settings","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Cutoff-Parameters","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Cutoff Parameters","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"SVD cutoff: 1e-10 (default)\nControls numerical precision\nSmaller cutoffs = higher accuracy but more memory","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#System-Size-Scaling","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"System Size Scaling","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"Memory: O(χ²d) where χ is bond dimension, d is physical dimension\nTime: O(Nχ³d²) for DMRG sweeps\nMeasurement application: O(Nχ³)","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Advanced-Usage","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Advanced Usage","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Custom-DMRG-Parameters","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Custom DMRG Parameters","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"function custom_ground_state(N; max_bond_dim=500, cutoff=1e-12)\n    sites = siteinds(\"Fermion\", N; conserve_qns=true)\n    H = fibonacci_hamiltonian_mps(sites)\n    \n    ψ₀ = randomMPS(sites, [\"0\" for _ in 1:N])\n    \n    sweeps = Sweeps(15)\n    setmaxdim!(sweeps, 50, 100, 200, max_bond_dim)\n    setcutoff!(sweeps, cutoff)\n    \n    energy, ψ = dmrg(H, ψ₀, sweeps)\n    return ψ, energy\nend","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Bulk-Measurement-with-Custom-Pattern","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Bulk Measurement with Custom Pattern","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"function custom_bulk_measurement(ψ, sites, N, τ, pattern)\n    current_state = copy(ψ)\n    results = []\n    \n    for layer_sites in pattern\n        layer_result = []\n        for site in layer_sites\n            ψ_p, prob_p = apply_measurement_mps(current_state, sites, site, τ, :p)\n            # Apply measurement based on probability or deterministic choice\n            # ... custom logic here\n        end\n        push!(results, layer_result)\n    end\n    \n    return results\nend","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Error-Handling-and-Debugging","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Error Handling and Debugging","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Common-Issues","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Common Issues","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"Bond dimension too small: Increase maxdim in DMRG\nNumerical instability: Decrease cutoff parameters\nMemory issues: Reduce bond dimension or system size\nSlow convergence: Increase number of DMRG sweeps","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Validation","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Validation","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"Check state normalization: abs(inner(ψ, ψ) - 1.0) < 1e-10\nVerify probability conservation: prob_p + prob_m ≈ 1.0\nMonitor bond dimensions: linkdims(ψ)","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Integration-with-Existing-Code","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Integration with Existing Code","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"The MPS implementation is designed to complement the existing exact diagonalization code:","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"# Compare exact vs MPS for small systems\nN = 8\nτ = 1.0\n\n# Exact method (using existing functions)\nexact_basis = Fibonacci_basis(N)\nexact_gs = # ... your existing ground state calculation\n\n# MPS method\nψ_mps, energy_mps = fibonacci_mps_ground_state(N)\n\n# Compare results\nprintln(\"Energy difference: $(energy_exact - energy_mps)\")","category":"page"},{"location":"mps_guide/#Future-Extensions","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"Future Extensions","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"mps_guide/","page":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","title":"MPS-based Fibonacci Chain Implementation","text":"Time evolution: Implement TEBD or other time evolution methods\nFinite temperature: Add finite temperature MPS algorithms\nDisorder: Include random disorder in the Hamiltonian\nAdvanced measurements: Implement more complex measurement protocols\nOptimization: Further optimize for specific Fibonacci chain properties","category":"page"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Documentation for FibonacciChain.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"","category":"page"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain.apply_measurement_mps-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, Any, Int64, Float64, Int64}","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain.apply_measurement_mps","text":"apply_measurement_mps(ψ::MPS, sites, i::Int, τ::Float64, sign::Int64; pbc::Bool=true) -> MPS, Float64\n\nApply measurement operator to MPS state and return the resulting state and probability.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain.ee_mps-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, Int64}","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain.ee_mps","text":"calculate_entanglement_entropy_mps(ψ::MPS, b::Int) -> Float64\n\nCalculate entanglement entropy of MPS state with bipartition at bond b.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain.fibonacci_hamiltonian_mps-Tuple{Any}","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain.fibonacci_hamiltonian_mps","text":"fibonacci_hamiltonian_mps(sites; pbc::Bool=true) -> MPO\n\nCreate Fibonacci chain Hamiltonian as an MPO using ITensor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain.initial_mps-Tuple{Int64}","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain.initial_mps","text":"fibonacci_mps_ground_state(N::Int; pbc::Bool=true) -> MPS\n\nGenerate the ground state of Fibonacci chain as an MPS.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain.measurement_operator_mps-Tuple{Any, Int64, Float64, Int64}","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain.measurement_operator_mps","text":"measurement_operator_mps(sites, i::Int, τ::Float64, sign::Int64; pbc::Bool=true) -> MPO\n\nCreate measurement operator at site i with parameter τ as an MPO.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain.mps_boundary_measure-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, Any, Vector{Int64}, Float64}","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain.mps_boundary_measure","text":"mps_boundary_measure(ψ::MPS, sites, measurement_sites::Vector{Int}, τ::Float64; \n            num_samples::Int=1000, pbc::Bool=true) -> Vector{Vector{Int64}}, Vector{Float64}\n\nPerform boundary measurements on MPS state.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain.mps_bulk_measurement-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, Any, Int64, Float64, Int64}","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain.mps_bulk_measurement","text":"mps_bulk_measurement(ψ::MPS, sites, N::Int, τ::Float64, D::Int; pbc::Bool=true)\n\nPerform bulk measurements on MPS with D layers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#FibonacciChain.mps_measurement_enumeration-Tuple{ITensorMPS.MPS, Any, Vector{Int64}, Float64}","page":"Home","title":"FibonacciChain.mps_measurement_enumeration","text":"mps_measurement_enumeration(ψ::MPS, sites, measurement_sites::Vector{Int}, τ::Float64; \n                           pbc::Bool=true) -> Vector{MPS}, Vector{Vector{Int64}}, Vector{Float64}\n\nEnumerate all possible measurement trajectories on MPS state.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"}]
